  "title": "Rules, London’s oldest restaurant, donated to National Trust",
  "summary": "Historic eatery in London’s Covent Garden, the oldest restaurant in the city, has been given to a heritage charity to protect its cultural and historical significance. The restaurant, which has changed hands only three times in over 228 years, now serves its food with a focus on the city’s past and traditions.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Rules, the oldest restaurant in London’s theatreland, has changed hands only three times in 228 years.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The restaurant’s interior, stuffed with historical playbills and vintage caricatures, is little changed from the 19th century.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The restaurant’s menu features traditional dishes like rabbit rillettes and roast guinea fowl.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
